SUMMARY:Trans Magic: Owning Our Stories of Strength and Resilience
DESCRIPTION:August 6 – 30\, 2026\nPetaluma Historical Library & Museum\n20 4th Street (Corner of 4th & B Street)\nHours:  Thursday – Sunday\,  10 a.m. – 4 p.m.\nAdmission Free\,  Donations Appreciated \n\n\nA community-curated exhibit celebrating the creativity\, organizing\, and history of trans and gender-expansive people in the North Bay and greater Bay Area. The exhibit traces a direct line from the gender-bending creativity of early 20th-century Vaudeville\, to the radical resistance of the groundbreaking 1966 Compton’s Cafeteria Riot\, and finally to the modern triumphs of community groups bringing joyful connection today. \nTrans Magic! Exhibit Opening Party\nSaturday\, August 8\, 2:00 – 4:00 pm\nPetaluma Historical Library & Museum\n20 4th Street (Corner of 4th & B Street)\nSliding scale donations support our Exhibit!\n\n\n\n\nFeaturing Exhibit Tours\, Music with DJ EM BASS\, Community\, Dancing!
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/trans-magic-owning-our-stories-of-strength-and-resilience/
LOCATION:Petaluma Historical Library & Museum\, 20 4th St\, Petaluma\, CA\, United States
CATEGORIES:Current Exhibit
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/TransMagic.png
END:VEVENT
